      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Recent claims that \"diseases of Western civilization\" are rare in rural African communities may not be justified. African peasants have a high pain threshold; many attend traditional healers rather than Western-trained doctors; and their language contains no words to express the descriptive terms used in Western medicine for the symptoms and clinical features of these diseases."},
